407 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 111 0 R
/T (This slide summarizes our Do's and Don'ts, practical guidelines to keep our designs consistent  and professional.)
/E (This slide summarizes our Do's and Don'ts, practical guidelines to keep our designs consistent  and professional.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
408 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 111 0 R
/T (Let's start with the Do's. Use black or white for most body text. It's always readable, and you never have to second-guess it .)
/E (Let's start with the Do's. Use black or white for most body text. It's always readable, and you never have to second-guess it .)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
409 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 111 0 R
/T (Use dark overlays on photos when placing text over images. A black overlay at 40 to 60 percent  opacity creates the contrast you need for readability.)
/E (Use dark overlays on photos when placing text over images. A black overlay at 40 to 60 percent  opacity creates the contrast you need for readability.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
410 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 111 0 R
/T (And lastly use color fades and accents only within our brand palette.      If it's not an approved color, don't use it. And always use the correct dimensions for each platform.)
/E (And lastly use color fades and accents only within our brand palette.      If it's not an approved color, don't use it. And always use the correct dimensions for each platform.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
411 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 111 0 R
