1828 0 obj
<<
/Title (Let's start with the Do's. Use black or white for most body text. It's always readable, and you never have to second-guess it .)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1816 0 R
/Prev 1823 0 R
/Next 1832 0 R
>>
endobj
1829 0 obj
<<
/Title (Don't use muted Gold for small areas of text like social media content. It's hard to read. Muted  Gold is meant for accents, not paragraphs.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1816 0 R
/Prev 1833 0 R
/Next 1824 0 R
>>
endobj
1830 0 obj
<<
/Title (Correct dimensions for each platform)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1807 0 R
/Prev 1826 0 R
/Next 1831 0 R
>>
endobj
1831 0 obj
<<
/Title (Colors outside the palette)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1807 0 R
/Prev 1830 0 R
/Next 1827 0 R
>>
endobj
1832 0 obj
<<
/Title (Use dark overlays on photos when placing text over images. A black overlay at 40 to 60 percent  opacity creates the contrast you need for readability.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1816 0 R
/Prev 1828 0 R
/Next 1834 0 R
>>
endobj
1833 0 obj
<<
/Title (Now the Don'ts. Don't use colors outside this palette. Even if a color looks appealing, consistency matters more  than variety.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1816 0 R
/Prev 1834 0 R
/Next 1829 0 R
>>
endobj
1834 0 obj
<<
/Title (And lastly use color fades and accents only within our brand palette.      If it's not an approved color, don't use it. And always use the correct dimensions for each platform.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1816 0 R
/Prev 1832 0 R
/Next 1833 0 R
>>
endobj
